timestamp=2026-11-04T12:37:21.580Z level=INFO run=56dc2648 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Analyze all dispatches for spoilage risk\nimport csv\n\n# Build products\nproducts = {}\nwith open('/app/dataset/product_catalog.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        pid = row['product_id']\n        try:\n            price = float(row['unit_price'].replace(',', '.'))\n        except:\n            price = float(row['unit_price'])\n        try:\n            w = float(row['unit_weight_kg'])\n        except:\n            w = float(row['unit_weight_kg'].replace(',', '.'))\n        try:\n            maxs = float(row['max_safe_temp_c'].replace(',', '.'))\n        except:\n            try:\n                maxs = float(row['max_safe_temp_c'])\n            except:\n                maxs = None\n        products[pid] = {\n            'cat': row['storage_category'],\n            'price': price,\n            'w': w,\n            'maxs': maxs\n        }\n\n# Build temperature series per zone (by timestamp)\ntemps = {}\nwith open('/app/dataset/temperature_logs.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        z = row['zone']\n        t = float(row['temperature_c'].replace(',', '.'))\n        ts = row['timestamp']\n        temps[(ts, z)] = t\n\n# Map zone name to category\n# Categories: Frozen, Meat, Dairy, Dry\n# Also see variations: frozen vs Frozen, dairy vs Dairy\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
