timestamp=2026-11-04T12:37:47.360Z level=INFO run=56dc2648 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Now examine each dispatch - what was the temperature at/around dispatch time?\n# Temperature readings are every 2 hours. A dispatch happens at some specific timestamp.\n# Did the product experience unsafe temps that would cause spoilage? If so, likely all units in that batch dispatched around that time are affected.\n\nimport csv\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\n# Build everything\nproducts = {}\nwith open('/app/dataset/product_catalog.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        pid = row['product_id']\n        try:\n            price = float(row['unit_price'].replace(',', '.'))\n        except:\n            price = float(row['unit_price'].replace(',', '.'))\n        try:\n            w = float(row['unit_weight_kg'])\n        except:\n            w = float(row['unit_weight_kg'].replace(',', '.'))\n        try:\n            maxs = float(row['max_safe_temp_c'].replace(',', '.'))\n        except:\n            maxs = None\n        products[pid] = {\n            'cat': row['storage_category'],\n            'price': price,\n            'w': w,\n            'maxs': maxs\n        }\n\nzone_readings = {}  # (ts, z) -> t\nwith open('/app/dataset/temperature_logs.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        z = row['zone']\n        t = float(row['temperature_c'].replace(',', '.'))\n        zone_readings[(ts_key := row['timestamp']), z] = t\n\nzone_map_cat = {\n    'Frozen': 'Frozen',\n    'frozen': 'Frozen',\n    'Meat': 'Meat',\n    'Dairy': 'Dairy',\n    'dairy': 'Dairy',\n    'Dry': 'Dry'\n}\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
