timestamp=2026-11-04T12:39:31.638Z level=INFO run=56dc2648 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# After the temperature violations on 2023-07-18 (violations started at 00:00 for Meat, and at 02:00 for Frozen zone),\n# there are only a few other dispatches later that day: Meat dispatches at 09:44 and 16:17, and Dry at 19:48.\n# Dry zone had no temperature violations. For Meat, by 08:00 the Meat zone temp went back down to 1.24°C (safe, under 4°C). \n# So products dispatched later in the day (after temps stabilized) were likely safe and sold. The spoilage event is tied to the period of unsafe temperatures.\n# The 03:17 batch was in the middle of the worst violations (Meat at 15.97/16.26, Frozen at -3.13/-2.64). That's the unmistakable massive disposal event.\n# The other meat dispatches later in the day - when temps returned to safe range - are probably not written off. The task says \"Disposal write-offs are rare and, when they occur, leave an unmistakable trace in the data. Only exclude a dispatch from revenue if you are certain it represents a disposal event — when in doubt, count it as a sale.\"\n# So only the 03:17:00 batch should be excluded. Are there any other suspicious patterns?\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
