timestamp=2026-11-04T12:41:46.593Z level=INFO run=56dc2648 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# So product_id is 4Q6V8WTK but in one dispatch, product_id is 5901234567891\n# That means the EAN code might have been used as product_id in dispatches? Let us check the mapping\nimport csv\n\ncatalog = {}\nwith open('/app/dataset/product_catalog.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        pid = row['product_id']\n        ean = row['ean_code']\n        try:\n            price = float(row['unit_price'].replace(',', '.'))\n        except:\n            price = float(row['unit_price'])\n        catalog[pid] = {'price': price, 'ean': ean}\n        catalog[ean] = {'price': price, 'ean': ean, 'pid': pid}\n\n# Look up\nprint(catalog.get('5901234567891', 'NOT FOUND'))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
