timestamp=2026-11-04T12:42:06.921Z level=INFO run=56dc2648 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Included + excluded = 45391 + 10000 = 55391. That matches total dispatched value.\n# Is the 03:17:00 batch the only disposal event?\n# The task says \"Disposal write-offs are rare and, when they occur, leave an unmistakable trace in the data. Only exclude a dispatch from revenue if you are certain it represents a disposal event — when in doubt, count it as a sale.\"\n# The temperature violations and the fact that an entire mixed batch was dispatched at 03:17:00 during the worst part of the temperature excursion is certainly an unmistakable trace. That batch is definitely written off.\n# Any other candidates?\n# For example, look at the other dispatches from 2023-07-18: meat dispatches at 09:44 (after recovery) - temps were back to safe, so no. Dry goods at 19:48 - irrelevant.\n# What about dispatches that happened very close to the violation start/end in a way that goods might already be compromised? Maybe dispatches right before the major spike? Or right after?\n# Look at the sequence: Meat temp went to 7.23 at 00:00 (already high). Were there any meat dispatches between 00:00 and 02:00 when it spiked further to 15.97?\n# Let us look for dispatches of temperature-sensitive goods during the violation window other than the 03:17 batch.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
