timestamp=2026-11-04T12:43:15.547Z level=INFO run=56dc2648 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Only those two frozen violations on 07-18, same window. Meat violations only on 07-18 in that window. No other violations anywhere else.\n# Also check if there are any other dispatches of frozen/meat that coincide temporally with any violation? Only the 03:17 batch. So seems the only disposal is that entire batch.\n# Also the task says \"warehouse management system and IoT sensors continued operating without interruption\" - so sensor data is reliable. That supports using temperature data as the unmistakable trace.\n\n# Another possibility: sometimes \"disposal write-offs\" might be recorded differently? But the data provided doesn't show explicit disposal records. The only data sources are product catalog, temperature logs, and warehouse dispatches. So we must infer disposals from those. The only strong signal is the temperature excursion coinciding with dispatches of sensitive goods in the affected zones - the 03:17 batch is the only case where everything lines up as a certain disposal.\n# That gives excluded = 10000 PLN. So expected revenue is 55391 - 10000 = 45391 PLN.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
